<title>SWEDEN: Volvo sees higher N.America truck sales.</title>
<headline>Volvo sees higher N.America truck sales.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish vehicle maker AB Volvo's truck division said on Tuesday it raised its forecast for total truck sales on the North American market to 200,000 per year from 188,000.  </p>
<p>&quot;We have raised our forecast to 200,000 trucks in 1997 from our earlier forecast of 188,000 trucks,&quot; company spokesman Stefan Lorentzson told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;It is the second time we have raised our forecast for the North American market this year. The U.S. economy is stronger than anyone believed previously.&quot;</p>
<p>Volvo did not want to comment on its own sales in North America but said so far this year the company had secured a 9.5 percent share of the market.</p>
<p>From January to May Volvo delivered 7,900 trucks to the North American market.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 101</p>
